<title>GERMANY: Siemens sees higher profit at Nixdorf.</title>
<headline>Siemens sees higher profit at Nixdorf.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>German electronics and engineering giant Siemens AG said it expects higher sales, profit and orders at Siemens-Nixdorf Informationssysteme AG computers unit.</p>
<p>Siemens officials told the annual news conference the company expects to cut about 6,000 domestic jobs in 1996/97.</p>
<p>Siemens sees restructuring costs remaining at about 500 million to 700 million marks over the next few years, they said.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
</text>
